solution:
We are told: Earth circumference at equator = 25,100 miles. Latitude of Lena = 45° N. Need circumference of circle of latitude through Lena. The radius of Earth = circumference/(2π) = 25100/(2π). The radius of the circle at latitude θ = R cosθ. For θ=45°, cos45° = √2/2 ≈ 0.7071. So circumference at latitude = 2π (R cos45°) = 2πR cos45° = (equator circumference) * cos45° = 25100 * 0.7071... ≈ 17700 (since 25100 * 0.7071 = 17748.21, nearest hundred is 17700). Answer key says 17700. So final answer is 17700.

The circumference at latitude 45° equals the equatorial circumference times the cosine of 45°.  Using 25,100 miles, the result is approximately 17,700 miles to the nearest hundred.

\boxed{17700}

