The lattice shown is continued for $9$ rows. What will be the third number in the $9$th row? \begin{tabular}{rccccc}
Row 1: & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 & 5 \\
Row 2: & 6 & 7 & 8 & 9 & 10 \\
Row 3: & 11 & 12 & 13 & 14 & 15 \\
Row 4: & 16 & 17 & 18 & 19 & 20
\end{tabular}

solution:
The lattice has 5 numbers per row, increasing by 1 each entry. Row 1 starts at 1, row 2 at 6, row 3 at 11, row 4 at 16, so each row starts at 5*(row-1)+1. For row 9, start = 5*(9-1)+1 = 5*8+1 = 40+1=41. The third number is start+2 = 41+2=43. The answer is 43.

The third number in row 9 is 43.

\boxed{43}

